<header><h1>The Universities of Jol&ndash;Nar</h1></header>
<article>
<h2 id="fragile"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Fragile">Fragile</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <sc>Fragile</sc> ability does not affect anti&ndash;fighter barrage, bombardment or space cannon rolls.<sup>1,2</sup></li>
    <li>The effect of the <sc>Fragile</sc> ability is mandatory.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="brilliant"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Brilliant">Brilliant</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When using Brilliant, the Jol&ndash;Nar player spends only the command token from their strategy pool, not the four resources. They then resolve the primary ability of the <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> strategy card, and may research an additional technology by spending six resources.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>When the Jol&ndash;Nar player uses <sc>Brilliant</sc>, they may research a second technology by spending six resources, without spending an additional command token.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="analytical"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Analytical">Analytical</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="research-agreement"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Research%20Agreement">Research Agreement</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Jol&ndash;Nar player will research several technologies in a row, then after each, the player holding <i>Research Agreement</i> may play it. The Jol&ndash;Nar player does not decide the next technology they will research until after the player holding the <i>Research Agreement</i> plays it or declines to.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If a player receives <i>Research Agreement</i> in a transaction immediately after the Jol&ndash;Nar player researched a technology, that player may play it immediately to gain that technology.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Once a player has used <i>Research Agreement</i> after the Jol&ndash;Nar player researches a technology, no other player may use <i>Research Agreement</i> for that same Jol&ndash;Nar research instance to gain the same technology.<sup>1</sup></li>
        <li>If the active player received the <i>Research Agreement</i> on a previous turn, they may play it and immediately perform a transaction with the Jol&ndash;Nar player to regain it. They may then play it when the Jol&ndash;Nar player researches their next technology.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Any deal between the Jol&ndash;Nar player and another player regarding when <i>Research Agreement</i> will be played, if made before <i>Research Agreement</i> is exchanged, is non&ndash;binding.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>If a faction has a faction&ndash;specific unit upgrade as one of their faction technologies, they cannot gain that unit upgrade from <i>Research Agreement</i> when the Jol&ndash;Nar player researches the generic version of that unit upgrade.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li><i>Research Agreement</i> may be triggered when the Jol&ndash;Nar player researches a technology outside of the <a href="/R_technology_sc"><i>Technology</i></a> strategy card. For example, it may be triggered by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Divert%20Funding"><i>Divert Funding</i></a> action card, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Focused%20Research"><i>Focused Research</i></a> action card, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Reveal%20Prototype"><i>Reveal Prototype</i></a> action card, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Technology%20Rider"><i>Technology Rider</i></a> action card, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Ixthian%20Artifact"><i>Ixthian Artifact</i></a> agenda, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Wormhole%20Research"><i>Wormhole Research</i></a> agenda, or the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Exploration#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Enigmatic%20Device"><i>Enigmatic Device</i></a> exploration card.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li><i>Research Agreement</i> cannot be triggered by a game effect that instructs the Jol&ndash;Nar player to directly gain a technology, without researching. For example, it cannot be triggered by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Fires%20of%20the%20Gashlai"><i>Fires of the Gashlai</i></a> <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> faction promissory note, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Plagiarize"><i>Plagiarize</i></a> action card, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#New_Agendas:~:text=Research%20Grant%20Reallocation"><i>Research Grant Reallocation</i></a> agenda, or the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Maw%20of%20Worlds"><i>Maw of Worlds</i></a> relic.<sup>2</sup></li>
        <li><i>Research Agreement</i> cannot be triggered when the Jol&ndash;Nar player resolves <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Leaders:~:text=Genetic%20Memory"><i>Genetic Memory</i></a>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="eres-siphons"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Faction_Technologies:~:text=E-Res%20Siphons">E&ndash;Res Siphons</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>E&ndash;Res Siphons</i> ability is triggered when the system is activated, even if the active player will perform no hostile acts toward the Jol&ndash;Nar player this turn.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If an effect other than activating a system during a tactical action places a command token in a system with the Jol&ndash;Nar player&rsquo;s ships (for example, the primary ability of the <a href="/R_diplomacy"><i>Diplomacy</i></a> strategy card), this will not cause <i>E&ndash;Res Siphons</i> ability to trigger.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="spatial-conduit-cylinder"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Spatial%20Conduit%20Cylinder">Spatial Conduit Cylinder</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Spatial Conduit Cylinder</i> is exhausted after the system is activated, before movement; the active system must already contain one of the Jol&ndash;Nar player&rsquo;s units.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The Jol&ndash;Nar player&rsquo;s PDS II units in systems made adjacent by <i>Spatial Conduit Cylinder</i> may use their <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> ability against the active system.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Other players may use the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/PDS#Upgraded_Unit:~:text=Deep%20Space%20Cannon"><sc>Deep Space Cannon</sc></a> ability of units in the same system as a Jol&ndash;Nar player&rsquo;s unit to produce hits during the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> step.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="j-n-s-hylarim"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Flagship:~:text=J.N.S.%20Hylarim">J.N.S. Hylarim</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Each result of 9 or 10 produces three hits in total: its normal hit and two additional hits.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="doctor-sucaban"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Leaders:~:text=Doctor%20Sucaban">Doctor Sucaban</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Jol&ndash;Nar player has the Infantry II unit upgrade, any of their infantry removed with Doctor Sucaban will not roll for resurrection.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="ta-zern"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Leaders:~:text=Ta%20Zern">Ta Zern</a> /<br/><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Leaders:~:text=Agnlan%20Oln">Agnlan Oln</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Ta Zern and Agnlan Oln work identically. Thunder&rsquo;s Edge replaces Ta Zern with Agnlan Oln because the <a href="/F_deepwrought">Deepwrought</a> player&rsquo;s hero is also named Ta Zern.<sup>2,7</sup></li>
    <li>The unit abilities that roll dice, and whose dice may be rerolled with this ability, are <a href="/R_anti_fighter_barrage"><sc>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</sc></a>, <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> and <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a>.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>&ldquo;Combat&rdquo; is a unit attribute, not a unit ability; this commander cannot reroll combat dice.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>This commander cannot be used to reroll dice for an Infantry II resurrection ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="rin-the-masters-legacy"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Leaders:~:text=Rin%2C%20The%20Master%27s%20Legacy">Rin, The Master&rsquo;s Legacy</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Leaders:~:text=Genetic%20Memory">Genetic Memory</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Jol&ndash;Nar player does not have to meet the prerequisites of the technologies they acquire.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>All replacements happen simultaneously. If this ability returns a specific technology, it cannot then be regained via this ability.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>If the Jol&ndash;Nar player later gains a technology they returned, they gain it readied.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the Jol&ndash;Nar player has the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note in their play area, they will not draw any action cards from the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Leaders:~:text=Nekro%20Acidos">Nekro Acidos</a> commander when they resolve <i>Genetic Memory</i>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If this ability is used to replace a faction technology which is currently being copied by the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> technology, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator">Valefar Assimilator</a> token stays on that technology while it is in the technology deck, and <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> still has that technology&rsquo;s text.<sup>4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="shield-paling"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Mech:~:text=Shield%20Paling">Shield Paling</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Shield Paling itself is still affected by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Fragile"><sc>Fragile</sc></a> ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="specialized-compounds"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Universities_of_Jol-Nar#Breakthrough:~:text=Specialized%20Compounds">Specialized Compounds</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Due to the synergy of <i>Specialized Compounds</i>, the Jol&ndash;Nar player may exhaust a planet with a yellow technology specialty to research a green technology, and vice versa.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>A technology with zero or completely ignored prerequisites must still match the color of the planet&rsquo;s technology specialty to use <i>Specialized Compounds</i>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The Jol&ndash;Nar player cannot use <i>Specialized Compounds</i> when researching a unit upgrade.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <ol><li>Unit upgrades do not have a color.<sup>1</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#Psychoarchaeology"><i>Psychoarchaeology</i></a> technology cannot be used to avoid exhausting the planet with the technology specialty.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>The Jol&ndash;Nar player cannot use a technology specialty planet to both pay for the research with <i>Specialized Compounds</i> and to ignore a prerequisite of the researched technology simultaneously.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
